<article>
	<h1><span>Tools Manager: Session Classes</span></h1>

	<ul class="nav">
		<li><a href="#overview">Overview</a></li>
		<li><a href="#column-headers">Column Headers</a></li>
		<li><a href="#toolbar">Toolbar</a></li>
		<li><a href="#sub-menu">Sub-menu Links</a></li>
	</ul>

	<section id="overview">
		<h2><span>Overview</span></h2>

		<p>Session classes can be managed here. Each class has an alias and a number of jobs allowed. Users assigned
			to a class are given its Jobs Allowed value, and changing a class's value updates them all. If no class
			exists when this screen opens, a class with the alias <em>default</em> and 3 jobs allowed is created.</p>
	</section>
	<section id="column-headers">
		<h2><span>Column Headers</span></h2>

		<dl>
			<dt>Checkbox</dt>
			<dd>Check this box to select one or more items. To select all items, check the box in the column heading.
				After one or more boxes are checked, click a toolbar button to take an action on the selected item or
				items.</dd>

			<dt>ID</dt>
			<dd>This is a unique identification number for this item assigned automatically by the system. Click it
				to edit the class.</dd>

			<dt>Alias</dt>
			<dd>The short name given to the class for easy identification. Click it to edit the class.</dd>

			<dt>Jobs Allowed</dt>
			<dd>The class's Jobs Allowed value.</dd>
		</dl>
	</section>
	<section id="toolbar">
		<h2><span>Toolbar</span></h2>
		<p>At the top right you will see the toolbar.</p>
		<p>The functions are:</p>
		<dl>
			<dt>New</dt>
			<dd>Opens the editing screen to create a new session class.</dd>

			<dt>Edit</dt>
			<dd>Opens the editing screen for the selected class. If more than one class is selected, only the first
				one is opened.</dd>

			<dt>Delete</dt>
			<dd>After asking for confirmation, permanently deletes the selected classes. Users in a deleted class are
				moved to the <em>default</em> class. The <em>default</em> class cannot be deleted: when it is selected,
				a warning is shown and deleting stops there.</dd>

			<dt>Help</dt>
			<dd>Opens this help screen.</dd>
		</dl>
	</section>
	<section id="sub-menu">
		<h2><span>Sub-menu Links</span></h2>
		<p>At the top left, you will see sub-menu options. These are links to managing various aspects of the tool
			environment. The links are:</p>
		<dl>
			<dt>Pipeline</dt>
			<dt>Hosts</dt>
			<dt>Host Types</dt>
			<dt>Zones</dt>
			<dd>Shown only when zones are turned on in the component's options.</dd>
			<dt>Sessions (this page)</dt>
			<dt>User Preferences</dt>
			<dt>File Handlers</dt>
		</dl>
		<p>Below them, a second row of links chooses what to show under Sessions:</p>
		<dl>
			<dt>Active</dt>
			<dt>Session classes (this page)</dt>
		</dl>
	</section>
</article>
